  "id": "COMPOUND:30176 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "Kaerophyllin is implicated in the interaction with A549 cells through a series of molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Kaerophyllin acts as a target for multiple compounds, including MOVP-3 and Licochalcone D, which in turn target A549 cells. This indicates a potential mechanism where Kaerophyllin may influence cellular processes through these intermediaries, ultimately affecting A549 cell behavior. The shared involvement of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One as a common target across these pathways suggests a possible role in mediating the effects of Kaerophyllin on A549 cells. The integration of these findings highlights a possible pathway where Kaerophyllin may modulate cellular responses via these intermediaries, contributing to its potential biological effects on A549 cells.",
